hyperWIN's own change to IronRDP, applied after ironrdp-keel.patch and ironrdp-hypermac.patch
(tools/vendor-ironrdp.sh).

- ironrdp-acceptor: CredSSP's credentials lookup (keel's) is given the domain the client sent
  too, as `domain\account`, not the account name alone. hyperWIN serves several VMs on one
  port, and with NLA the domain typed before the user name (`w10\admin`, or `admin@w10`) is
  the only place a client such as mstsc can say which VM it wants.

- ironrdp-vmconnect: the frame-buffer channel for a client that runs as a service. LocalSystem's
  token has no logon SID (what the client hello carries), so the channel never started and the
  session fell back to bitmap updates, quietly: some 360 partial updates a second instead of
  one whole frame per guest frame. Now the token's own user SID is sent then; a channel that
  cannot start says so (warn); and the shared buffer's mutex is held for a copy only, the
  pixel conversion happens after it is released.

